Z||000000||Old Lar||02-21-2001||06:21 PM||||The March 2000 issue of Smoke Signals has a two page article on Ot Huster's pure stock 84 silver coupe.  Ot's car usually wins at the Fiero shows, but has scored 398 out of 400 points at the POCI national shows for the past two years.  A comment made in the article was that 7 Fieros at the national show took home some honor consideing that there were only 8 or 9 Fieros at the national.||||reg||1
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||02-21-2001||11:59 PM||||Ot's 84 is simply AWESOME !!!!! MaryAnns 87 coupe is AWESOME too !!!||||reg||4
Z||000002||ChadMan||02-22-2001||09:16 AM||||Yeah, Ot's car is one-of-a-kind.  I haven't seen a nicer '84 since, well, 1984.<P>I first saw Ot's car at an all-Pontiac show at Dennis Pontiac (in 1994?).  He told me about FOCOA...before that, I thought I was the only person on Earth who liked these little cars.  If it weren't for Ot, I'd probably be driving a CRX right now.||||reg||7
